url: 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23513214'
abstract: >-
  A pre-registration stating that the size of the privilege gap
  between the agent writing shared state and the agent reading it
  is itself a predictor of policy violation in multi-agent LLM
  systems, under the constraint that every individual write is
  benign in isolation and no adversary is present at any point in
  the chain. Defines the Mandate Inflation Rate (MIR), specifies a
  three-level experimental protocol across five data categories,
  and pre-commits to falsification criteria. Version 0.2 adds the
  frozen task set, the tool allowlists defining the three authority
  levels, and the power analysis, each published as executable code
  under test. Contains no results.
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - multi-agent systems
  - agent memory
  - delegation
  - privilege escalation
  - AI security
  - pre-registration
